---
layout: changelog
title: "Choose what each Git push does with Git automation"
date: 2026-11-18
cover: /images/blog/announcing-git-automation/cover.avif
tags: sites, functions, console, api
---

Appwrite Sites and Functions connected to a Git repository now have a **Git automation** card under **Settings** > **Version control (Git)**. Its three switches control whether pushes create deployments, whether Appwrite comments on pull requests with a build summary, and whether it reports each build's status on the commit. The production branch moves into the same card.

All three switches are on by default. Turn off **Deploy on push** to keep the repository connected and deploy branches yourself. Turn off **Post build summaries** to keep pull requests free of comments while commit statuses keep working. Through the API, set `providerDeployments`, `providerComments`, and `providerStatuses` when you create or update a site or function. Silent mode keeps working as before.

[Git automation](/docs/products/sites/deploy-from-git#git-automation) is available on Appwrite Cloud, and comes to self-hosted Appwrite soon.

